title: ActOneNotes
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The commission
style: note
---
Act I, two days in the village. Five landmarks for the map, three of them inside child scenes (the cellar under the inn, the mill's loft, the chapel's bell). Somebody moves the boundary stones at night. The steward and the miller quarrel over the road. The act ends when the survey and the stones are done, or on the night of the second day, when the Countess sends for the cartographer. #line:ActOneNotes_0100
===

title: Events
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The commission
quest: survey
when: once
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: here() == "Village"
---
The road comes down out of the hills, and there is Ashcombe. A river, a mill, a chapel, an inn, and the castle on the hill above them. #line:Events.3344e1f8_0100
You carry a letter with the seal of Countess Ysolde Varne. #line:Events.3344e1f8_0200
"Survey the village before the spring fair. Five landmarks, set down true. The hearing will want them." #line:Events.3344e1f8_0300
<<set $quest_survey to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed survey>>
===

title: Events
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The road
when: once
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: here() == "Village"
when: $met_corvin and $met_bram
---
// The first fork: the steward and the miller find each other in the square, with the cartographer between them.
Corvin: Ah. The miller has found you too. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0100_Corvin
Bram: Tell him, cartographer. Tell him the old road goes around the mill and always has. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0200_Bram
Corvin: The old road goes around everything. The new one will go straight, past the mill, and the castle's carts will thank us. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0300_Corvin
Bram: Past the mill? Through it! #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0400_Bram
-> Corvin is right. A straight road is a good road. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0500
    <<set $road to Road.Corvin>>
    Corvin: A sensible eye. The Countess will hear of it. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0600_Corvin
    Bram: Then draw your map, and draw my mill as a ruin while you are at it. #mood:angry #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0700_Bram
-> The road should go around the mill. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0800
    <<set $road to Road.Miller>>
    Bram: There. Even a stranger sees it. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_0900_Bram
    Corvin: A stranger who will be paid by the castle. Remember that. #mood:angry #line:Events.c5b2af3a_1000_Corvin
-> I draw what is there. Roads are for the hearing. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_1100
    <<set $road to Road.NoSide>>
    Corvin: Careful. Nobody pays for a map that says nothing. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_1200_Corvin
    Bram: Nobody pays a miller either. #line:Events.c5b2af3a_1300_Bram
===

title: Events
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The moving stones
quest: herbs
when: once
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: $quest_herbs == QuestState.Active and not $dewcup_taken
when: day() > 2 or (day() == 2 and time_of_day() != "morning")
---
// The dew-cup only opens in the morning: after the morning of the second day, it is too late.
The dew-cups by the river have closed for the year. Nan will have to make do. #line:Events.2e45e09b_0100
<<set $quest_herbs to QuestState.Failed>>
<<quest_changed herbs>>
===

title: Events
act: Survey
location: Anywhere
scenario: The commission
when: once
when: $act == Act.Survey
when: ($quest_survey == QuestState.Succeeded and $quest_stones == QuestState.Succeeded) or day() > 2 or (day() == 2 and time_of_day() == "night")
---
// The end of the first act: the Countess sends for the cartographer. The road to the castle is a journey, held until
// this dialogue ends, wherever in the village the cartographer is.
A rider in the castle's colours comes down the road and stops at your side. #line:Events.b5e3bbae_0100
Rider: The Countess will see the cartographer. Now, with the map as it is. #line:Events.b5e3bbae_0200_Rider
<<if $quest_survey != QuestState.Succeeded>>
    You look at the map. [plural value={survey_count()} one="One landmark" other="% landmarks" /] out of five. It will have to do. #line:Events.b5e3bbae_0300
    <<set $quest_survey to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed survey>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_stones != QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<if $culprit == Culprit.Unknown>>
        <<set $culprit to Culprit.Pell>>
    <<endif>>
    Maren: The stones moved again last night. I have my man. The peddler. Strangers always. #mood:angry #line:Events.b5e3bbae_0400_Maren
    <<set $quest_stones to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed stones>>
<<endif>>
<<set $act to Act.Castle>>
<<set $pell_in_village to false>>
<<set $pell_at_castle to true>>
<<set $corvin_in_village to false>>
<<set $corvin_at_castle to true>>
<<end_day>>
<<go CastleRoad>>
===

title: CastleRoad
act: Survey
location: Village
scenario: The commission
when: $act == Act.Survey
---
The road climbs to the castle. The Countess expects you when the survey is done, not before. #line:CastleRoad.d3a83dcf_0100
===

title: CastleRoad
act: Fair
location: Village
scenario: The hearing
when: $act == Act.Fair
---
Not today. The whole valley is coming down this road for the fair. #line:CastleRoad.310c4248_0100
===

title: MineRoad
act: All
location: Anywhere
scenario: Under the hill
when: $act != Act.Mine
---
A miner sits on a rock across the path. #line:MineRoad.4970268d_0100
Miner: The mine is no place for visitors. Turn back. #line:MineRoad.4970268d_0200_Miner
===
